          ],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "Great options in Singapore, depending on how fast you want to be seen and whether you prefer a hospital-based team or a private clinic:\n\nHospital-based sports medicine (best if you may need imaging/specialists; subsidised if you have a polyclinic/CHAS GP referral)\n- SSMC @ CGH (Changi General Hospital, Simei) \u2013 Singapore\u2019s largest multidisciplinary sports medicine centre with sports physiotherapy. ([cgh.com.sg](https://www.cgh.com.sg/our-specialties/ssmccgh?utm_source=openai))\n- SSMC @ Novena (Novena Medical Centre) \u2013 multidisciplinary team including sports physiotherapists. ([cgh.com.sg](https://www.cgh.com.sg/ssmc/about-ssmc/facilities?utm_source=openai))\n- Singapore General Hospital \u2013 Orthopaedic Sports & Joint Centre with physiotherapy support. ([sgh.com.sg](https://www.sgh.com.sg/our-specialties/orthopaedic-sports-and-joint-centre?utm_source=openai))\n- NUH Sports Centre (Kent Ridge) \u2013 includes Sports Physiotherapy. ([nuh.com.sg](https://www.nuh.com.sg/care-at-nuh/services/orthopaedic-surgery/nuh-sports-centre?utm_source=openai))\n\nPrivate clinics (fast access; no referral needed; widespread locations)\n- Core Concepts Physiotherapy \u2013 multi-location musculoskeletal/sports physio. ([coreconceptsphysio.sg](https://www.coreconceptsphysio.sg/?utm_source=openai))\n- PhysioActive \u2013 sports physiotherapy and performance. ([physioactive.sg](https://physioactive.sg/?utm_source=openai))\n- City Osteopathy & Physiotherapy \u2013 several centres; lists first-session physio fee (~$210 before GST). ([cityosteophysio.com](https://cityosteophysio.com/contact-us/?utm_source=openai))\n- UFIT Physiotherapy (Orchard, one-north) \u2013 integrated rehab gym; price list shows $200\u2013$280 depending on session/therapist. ([ufit.com.sg](https://www.ufit.com.sg/health/physiotherapy?utm_source=openai))\n- BMJ Physiotherapy \u2013 includes a Sports Hub (Kallang) sports injury clinic. ([bmjtherapy.com](https://bmjtherapy.com/sports-hub-kallang/?utm_source=openai))\n- Physio & Sole Clinic \u2013 integrated physiotherapy plus podiatry; many locations (useful for foot/ankle/running issues). ([physioandsole.com.sg](https://physioandsole.com.sg/?utm_source=openai))\n- Singapore Physio \u2013 sports-focused physiotherapy. ([singaporephysio.com](https://www.singaporephysio.com/services/sports-physiotherapy/?utm_source=openai))\n\nHow to choose quickly\n- Proximity and availability: pick somewhere you can visit consistently in the next 4\u20136 weeks.\n- Sport/injury match: runners/foot-ankle often benefit from clinics with in\u2011house podiatry (e.g., Physio & Sole). Complex or surgical cases do well in hospital centres (CGH/SGH/NUH). ([physioandsole.com.sg](https://physioandsole.com.sg/sports-podiatry-services-singapore/?utm_source=openai))\n- Budget/claims: private session fees commonly range about $200\u2013$280 for initial consults (examples above); some insurers require a doctor\u2019s referral to claim\u2014check your policy. ([ufit.com.sg](https://www.ufit.com.sg/hubfs/FOR%20ONLINE%20BOOKING%20PAGE.pdf?utm_source=openai))\n\nReferral basics in Singapore\n- Private clinics: you can book directly without a doctor\u2019s referral. ([ask.gov.sg](https://ask.gov.sg/sgh-ahpedia/questions/cmeqy6tpy00hzf2j1moutd9tk?utm_source=openai))\n- Public hospitals: typically need a doctor\u2019s referral (e.g., polyclinic) to access physiotherapy services and subsidies. ([cgh.com.sg](https://www.cgh.com.sg/our-specialties/rehabilitative-services/physio?utm_source=openai))\n\nIf you share your sport, injury (e.g., ACL, shoulder, back, runner\u2019s knee), preferred area (East/Central/West/North), and budget, I can narrow this to 2\u20133 specific clinics and the soonest slots near you."
